      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Save Webz.io news search results to Google Sheets\n\n**Self-hosted n8n only.** This template uses the `n8n-nodes-webz-news-search` community node, which cannot be installed on n8n Cloud.\n\n### Who's it for\n\nAnalysts, researchers, and ops teams who want news coverage as plain spreadsheet rows they can sort, filter, and chart. There is no AI model and no prompt to tune, so every run returns the same shape of data.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. You start the run from the manual trigger.\n2. **Search settings** holds the query, article count, and lookback window, so it is the only node you edit day to day.\n3. **Search Webz.io news** searches Webz.io global news and returns one item per article, with `title`, `url`, `published`, `score`, `excerpt`, and the `query` that found it.\n4. **Append articles to sheet** writes each article as its own row.\n\n### How to set up\n\n1. Install `n8n-nodes-webz-news-search` under **Settings \u2192 Community nodes**.\n2. On **Search Webz.io news**, add a **Webz.io News Search API** credential holding your API token.\n3. On **Append articles to sheet**, connect your Google account and pick your spreadsheet and tab.\n4. Give that tab these headers: `title`, `url`, `published`, `score`, `excerpt`, `query`.\n5. Edit **Search settings**, then run the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\n\n- Self-hosted n8n\n- A Webz.io API token from [webz.io](https://webz.io)\n- A Google account\n\n### How to customize\n\nReplace the manual trigger with a **Schedule Trigger** to build a rolling archive. Open **Additional Filters** on the search node for language, country, ticker, sentiment, domain, and category. Keep the search subject in **Query**: **Topic** is a separate enrichment filter, not a replacement for it.\n\n[Setup notes and full filter reference](https://github.com/Webhose/webz-news-search/blob/main/n8n/README.md)",
